<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine tax revenues said up in July and August.</title>
<headline>Argentine tax revenues said up in July and August.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine tax revenue for July and August was 14 percent higher than the same two months last year while for the first eight months of 1996 revenue was up five percent on 1995, a top official said Thursday.</p>
<p>Cabinet Chief Jorge Rodriguez was quoted by the state news agency Telam giving the tax figures after Thursday's weekly cabinet meeting. No further details were available.</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0695</p>
